WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:05.120
All these years you thought you knew&nbsp;
which character was the real antagonist&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:09.200
of "The Craft," but by the end of this video,&nbsp;
you’ll never see the movie the same way again.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:14.640
"The Craft" wastes no time in introducing&nbsp;
us to its principal characters.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.640 --> 00:00:18.800
The film opens on three young witches —&nbsp;
Nancy, Rochelle, and Bonnie — performing a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.800 --> 00:00:24.240
pagan ceremony. After a flashy opening credits&nbsp;
sequence, we meet protagonist Sarah Bailey,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:28.400
a San Francisco transplant who's recently&nbsp;
moved to Los Angeles with her father.

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:34.080
Sarah's first day in her new LA home takes a&nbsp;
frightening turn when a strange man holding a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:39.760
huge snake walks right through her front door&nbsp;
and presents it to her as some kind of twisted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:45.280
housewarming present. This doesn't seem to leave&nbsp;
Sarah too traumatized to start at her new Catholic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:50.000
school the following day — despite the fact&nbsp;
that she's yet to be fitted for a uniform.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.560
Elsewhere at school, Bonnie's astrological&nbsp;
readings predict the arrival of a newcomer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.560 --> 00:00:58.160
whom she interprets as being the&nbsp;
fourth member she and her friends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.160 --> 00:01:03.520
need to complete their circle — a sentiment&nbsp;
that Nancy wholeheartedly disagrees with.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:09.920
When Bonnie sees Sarah performing telekinesis with&nbsp;
a pencil in French class, she knows exactly who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.040
her reading was referring to. Despite Bonnie's&nbsp;
eagerness to induct Sarah into their coven,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.040 --> 00:01:21.680
Nancy scares Sarah away with a wordless glare when&nbsp;
she asks the trio if she can join their lab group.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:26.400
Sitting alone at lunch, Sarah is joined by popular&nbsp;
jock Chris Hooker, who welcomes her to the school.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:31.120
When she points out the girls that snubbed her&nbsp;
in biology, Chris calls them an offensive name&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:36.720
and warns Sarah to stay away because they're&nbsp;
infamous for being witches. Even though Sarah&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:41.920
is initially doubtful, she finds herself&nbsp;
intrigued by both Chris and the girls.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:47.680
After school, Sarah is watching Chris at football&nbsp;
practice when she's approached by Nancy, Rochelle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:52.960
and Bonnie. Noticing Sarah's interest in the&nbsp;
team captain, Nancy gives her a stern warning.

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:53.280
"He spreads disease. I speak&nbsp;
from personal experience."

00:01:53.280 --> 00:01:58.720
Sarah isn't sure what to think, but when the&nbsp;
girls invite her to go shopping with them,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.280
she finds herself compelled to join. On&nbsp;
their walk to the local occult store,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:08.560
Nancy notices scars on Sarah's wrists. Sarah&nbsp;
confesses that her family's relocation was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:12.320
spurred by an attempt she made on&nbsp;
her own life back in San Francisco.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:17.200
The responses from the girls are… less&nbsp;
than compassionate, to say the least.

00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:17.504
"You even did it the right way."
"Yeah."

00:02:17.504 --> 00:02:17.600
"Punk rock!"

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:22.560
The occult shop — run by the enigmatic&nbsp;
proprietor Lirio — is filled with all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:28.320
kinds of esoteric iconography. Just as Sarah is&nbsp;
about to open the curtain to a hidden backroom,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:31.280
Lirio stops her and gives her a quick reading. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.240
shop owner recognizes that Sarah's ring&nbsp;
previously belonged to her late mother&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:41.520
and tells the girl she has natural powers,&nbsp;
but Sarah takes this with a grain of salt.

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:46.960
On their way home, the same man who'd accosted&nbsp;
Sarah with a snake sees and chases her again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.600
only to be run over by a passing car.&nbsp;
Collecting their thoughts after the accident,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.760
the group comes to the conclusion that&nbsp;
their individual wishes for the man to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:01.280
stop willed the passing car into hitting him.&nbsp;
When Nancy starts explaining Manon — the deity&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:06.320
the girls worship — Sarah knows for sure&nbsp;
that her new friends aren't playing around.

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:06.640
"If God and the devil were playing football…&nbsp;
Manon would be the stadium that they played on."

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:10.960
Sarah admits that magical things seem&nbsp;
to happen to her all the time, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:14.320
she gets frightened by Nancy's&nbsp;
intensity and excuses herself.

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.840
After her whirlwind evening with&nbsp;
St. Benedict's resident witches,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.680
Sarah tries to take her mind off things by&nbsp;
agreeing to go out with Chris Hooker. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.680 --> 00:03:28.160
have a good time, but when she refuses to go&nbsp;
back to his house, Chris decides to spread a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:32.800
vile rumor around school that they'd actually&nbsp;
hooked up — and that it hadn't gone well.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.800 --> 00:03:37.680
She tries to confront Chris in the hallway but&nbsp;
only ends up getting humiliated even further.

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:42.000
In the meantime, Sarah's new friends are all&nbsp;
dealing with personal problems of their own.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.920
As one of the only Black students at St.&nbsp;
Benedict's, Rochelle has to put up with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:51.280
constant tormenting from a racist bully named&nbsp;
Laura and her gaggle of followers. Bonnie has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:55.360
burn scars all over her shoulders and&nbsp;
back from a childhood accident and is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.960
undergoing extremely painful experimental&nbsp;
gene therapy to try and remove them. Nancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:06.320
lives in a run-down trailer with her alcoholic&nbsp;
mother Grace and her abusive stepfather Ray.

00:04:06.320 --> 00:04:10.080
The next day, the three invite Sarah&nbsp;
on a field trip, which she accepts,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:12.560
and the group takes a bus&nbsp;
out to the desolate woods.

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:18.560
Deep in the woods, Sarah, Rochelle, Nancy,&nbsp;
and Bonnie begin a ceremony that officially&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.560 --> 00:04:24.800
establishes their circle; they hold each other&nbsp;
at knifepoint while reciting an incantation.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:25.200
"How do you enter?"
"With perfect love and perfect trust."

00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:29.680
The four witches then pierce their index&nbsp;
fingers and mix their blood with wine,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.680 --> 00:04:35.920
performing their first group spell. They each&nbsp;
drink in turn, asking Manon for what their hearts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.920 --> 00:04:42.400
desire. Rochelle wants revenge on Laura, Sarah&nbsp;
wants Chris to return her affections, and Bonnie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.400 --> 00:04:48.640
wants to be beautiful on the outside as well as&nbsp;
in. Nancy, however, dreams a little bit bigger.

00:04:48.640 --> 00:04:49.120
"...and I take into myself…&nbsp;
all the power of Manon."

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.280
Within a matter of hours, Sarah's&nbsp;
love spell on Chris begins working,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.280 --> 00:04:58.320
and she manipulates his new obsession&nbsp;
to humiliate him in retaliation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:03.280
The coven decides to further test their abilities&nbsp;
by playing "light as a feather, stiff as a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:09.200
board" — the result of which undoubtedly confirms&nbsp;
the presence of supernatural intervention.

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:15.280
The next day, when Laura bullies Rochelle, her&nbsp;
signature blonde coif immediately starts falling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.280 --> 00:05:22.000
out. Then, at her next doctor's appointment,&nbsp;
Bonnie's scars melt off her body with impossible&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:29.200
ease, leaving the doctor speechless. The magic&nbsp;
is working… for everyone but Nancy, that is.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.360
Frustrated by Manon's lack of intervention&nbsp;
until now, Nancy returns to her dysfunctional&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:40.800
family. But a violent encounter that ends&nbsp;
in her stepfather dying of a heart attack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:46.320
seems to prove that her prayers have not been&nbsp;
ignored after all. A life insurance policy leaves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:53.440
Nancy and her mother 175,000 dollars, which&nbsp;
they use to move into fancier digs downtown.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.440 --> 00:05:57.600
At Nancy's new apartment, the witches&nbsp;
practice "glamouring" — a type of spell&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.000
that can change outward appearances&nbsp;
with just a bit of concentration.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:06.320
All is not well in the witches' world,&nbsp;
however. Sarah's love spell seems to have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.320 --> 00:06:12.480
been too effective, turning Chris' newfound desire&nbsp;
into a dangerous obsession. Sarah consults Lirio&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.480 --> 00:06:17.520
for advice on how to break the spell, but she&nbsp;
learns an unfortunate truth about witchcraft:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:22.640
a spell must run its course. She also&nbsp;
learns about the law of karmic justice:

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:23.120
"Whatever you send out… you get back times three."

00:06:23.120 --> 00:06:26.640
At the beach at twilight, the&nbsp;
coven arrives with their familiars&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:31.840
as they prepare to invoke the spirit of Manon.&nbsp;
Here, Sarah opens up some more about her past:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.840 --> 00:06:36.400
specifically, that she used to hallucinate&nbsp;
snakes and insects around the time of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:42.080
suicide attempt. Unfazed, Nancy leads an&nbsp;
incredibly intense ceremony that provokes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:45.520
lightning and wind as the&nbsp;
women chant. The next morning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.520 --> 00:06:51.760
they awaken on the beach to find Nancy walking on&nbsp;
water and a horde of dead sharks washed ashore.

00:06:52.720 --> 00:06:58.080
Sarah — understandably freaked out by the&nbsp;
invocation ceremony — tries to talk sense into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.080 --> 00:07:03.040
the other three witches, but they're all drunk on&nbsp;
Nancy's power. Even though Rochelle experiences&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:08.560
some remorse when she sees Laura having a panic&nbsp;
attack over her balding scalp, it's three against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:13.920
one, and Nancy is starting to think that maybe&nbsp;
Sarah shouldn't be part of the coven after all.

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:19.360
Feeling lost and afraid, Sarah turns to Chris for&nbsp;
support, even though his obsession is reaching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.360 --> 00:07:24.800
dangerous levels. She agrees to go out with him&nbsp;
for dinner, but instead, Chris takes her to a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.800 --> 00:07:30.000
remote spot where he sexually assaults her. Sarah&nbsp;
manages to escape to Rochelle's house and tells&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:35.600
the other witches what happened, and in a fit of&nbsp;
rage, Nancy lures Chris upstairs at a nearby party&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:42.080
and glamours herself into Sarah. When the real&nbsp;
Sarah breaks the glamour and Chris is dismissive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:48.400
once again, Nancy loses it. She throws Chris out&nbsp;
a window with her mind, killing him instantly.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:53.360
In the wake of Chris' death — which&nbsp;
everyone conveniently thinks was an&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.360 --> 00:07:58.080
accident — Sarah breaks with the coven&nbsp;
entirely. She cuts Nancy out of a group&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:58.080 --> 00:08:02.720
photo and attempts to do a binding spell that&nbsp;
would prevent Nancy from hurting anyone else&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.720 --> 00:08:07.040
or herself. Unfortunately for Sarah,&nbsp;
the power of Manon has given Nancy the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.040 --> 00:08:12.080
ability to read her mind and torment her&nbsp;
with terrible dreams and hallucinations.

00:08:12.080 --> 00:08:16.800
At school, Nancy, Bonnie, and Rochelle accost&nbsp;
Sarah in the bathroom, telling her that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:22.080
were all interviewed by police following Chris'&nbsp;
death. Nancy argues that Ray and Chris deserved&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.080 --> 00:08:25.784
to die and that if Sarah wants to leave&nbsp;
the coven, she'd better watch her back.

00:08:25.784 --> 00:08:25.840
"If a witch betrayed her&nbsp;
coven… they would kill her."

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:29.760
Desperate, Sarah goes to Lirio at the&nbsp;
occult shop for help and explains her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.760 --> 00:08:35.040
predicament. Lirio invites Sarah into the&nbsp;
secret backroom — a pagan temple built on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:40.720
a "place of power." She lights all the candles&nbsp;
with one match and tells Sarah she's from a long&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:45.840
line of witches and needs to invoke Manon&nbsp;
herself. Before Lirio can help any further,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:45.840 --> 00:08:50.800
however, Nancy disrupts the ceremony&nbsp;
astrally, forcing Sarah to retreat home.

00:08:52.160 --> 00:08:56.400
Sarah arrives at an empty house and finds&nbsp;
out that her father and stepmother flew to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.440
San Francisco thinking that Sarah had run&nbsp;
away. Unbelievably, their plane crashed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:06.640
killing everyone on board. Just when Sarah&nbsp;
thinks things couldn't get any worse,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:06.640 --> 00:09:12.880
the house starts filling with snakes, bugs,&nbsp;
rats, and all sorts of creepy crawlies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.880 --> 00:09:16.480
The creatures chase Sarah until&nbsp;
she's face to face with Nancy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.480 --> 00:09:21.920
who reveals that the whole thing was a glamour and&nbsp;
that she's planning on staging Sarah's suicide.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:26.880
Desperate to fight back, Sarah is forced&nbsp;
to invoke the spirit of Manon herself.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:32.000
In the process, she gives Bonnie and Rochelle a&nbsp;
taste of their own medicine with the law of karma,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:34.320
and the two run away in fear.

00:09:34.320 --> 00:09:38.880
Sarah finishes invoking the spirit and&nbsp;
uses the opportunity to torment Nancy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.760
the same way she tormented her — using&nbsp;
all sorts of glamours and tricky spells.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:47.600
Nancy tries to kill Sarah, but&nbsp;
with her newly invoked powers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:52.800
Sarah is able to successfully bind&nbsp;
Nancy and end their showdown for good.

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:57.600
Days later, Bonnie and Rochelle visit Sarah&nbsp;
to apologize for their actions during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:02.720
confrontation. They reveal they've lost their&nbsp;
powers, but that doesn't stop Sarah from using&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.720 --> 00:10:08.240
her abilities to try and crush them with a tree&nbsp;
branch. Finally, "The Craft" ends with Nancy in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.240 --> 00:10:13.280
a mental institution shouting about the power&nbsp;
of Manon as she's being restrained and sedated.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.400
While "The Craft" is framed as a movie about&nbsp;
four young witches with new girl Sarah Bailey&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:21.200
at the center, over the years, the&nbsp;
discourse surrounding the film has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:21.200 --> 00:10:25.920
deepened considerably to propose the notion&nbsp;
that Sarah might in fact be the bad guy here.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.920 --> 00:10:30.640
For one, Sarah abandons her sisters on several&nbsp;
occasions to run back to Chris Hooker — the guy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:35.040
who spread a nasty rumor about her right&nbsp;
at the start. Even after Chris tries to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:40.160
sexually assault Sarah and Nancy kills him in&nbsp;
retaliation, Sarah still tries to defend him.

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:40.800
"I think that he was a good&nbsp;
guy underneath it all."

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.000
Say what?

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:45.200
By the end of "The Craft," when Sarah&nbsp;
has invoked the spirit of Manon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:49.840
instead of trying to help Nancy with her newfound&nbsp;
powers, she taunts her with the same manipulations&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:49.840 --> 00:10:54.800
that Nancy used on her, effectively driving&nbsp;
her mad by the film's end. She also ends the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.800 --> 00:10:59.040
film by threatening Bonnie and Rochelle even&nbsp;
after they confessed to losing their powers.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:10:59.440
"Be careful. You don't want to end up like Nancy."

00:10:59.440 --> 00:11:03.840
It seems as if Sarah took her powers to&nbsp;
as dark a place as Nancy's went — but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:06.400
for whatever reason, she's&nbsp;
allowed to get away with it.

00:11:07.520 --> 00:11:13.280
If Sarah is the actual villain of "The Craft,"&nbsp;
then we need to reassess her foil, Nancy Downs.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:13.280 --> 00:11:18.000
Nancy starts the film living in a trailer park&nbsp;
where her stepdad regularly abuses her alcoholic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:22.320
mother. Their electricity is often out since they&nbsp;
can't pay their bills, and there's even a hole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:27.040
in the roof over Nancy's bed, dripping water on&nbsp;
her face as she tries to sleep. The implication&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:27.040 --> 00:11:31.120
is that Nancy is a scholarship student at&nbsp;
the elite St. Benedict's Catholic school&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:36.240
and that she spends her free time casting spells&nbsp;
to try and lift her and her mother out of poverty.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:41.840
On top of all that, Nancy was given an STD and&nbsp;
abandoned by Chris Hooker, not to mention how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:41.840 --> 00:11:47.600
often Ray seems to violate her bodily autonomy.&nbsp;
The link between poverty, a lack of healthcare,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:52.160
and possible underlying mental illness,&nbsp;
combined with dabbling in the occult,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:57.600
was a devastating cocktail for Nancy: she wanted&nbsp;
the power to change her life and circumstances,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:02.240
but she didn't know how to do it without using&nbsp;
supernatural means. Even when she and her mom&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:07.920
come into a considerable amount of money, Nancy&nbsp;
still isn't able to address her root traumas.

00:12:08.480 --> 00:12:13.920
That said, "The Craft" has a far more ambiguous&nbsp;
ending than people think. Thanks to Sarah's spell,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:19.680
Nancy is only bound against hurting herself and&nbsp;
others — not against using magic as a whole. If&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:19.680 --> 00:12:25.040
she'd been able to gather her thoughts and regroup&nbsp;
internally, she could realize that she still has&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:29.840
access to Manon's power. This could change&nbsp;
her circumstances for the better once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:29.840 --> 00:12:35.360
even without violence. Furthermore, a spell only&nbsp;
lasts as long as the witch who cast it lives,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:40.480
so if Sarah dies before Nancy, Nancy could&nbsp;
be walking on water again in no time.

00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:45.680
On the surface, "The Craft" is a story&nbsp;
about young women coming into personal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:50.800
and collective power through magic. However,&nbsp;
this camaraderie only lasts briefly, and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:55.600
it's not long before the four women involved&nbsp;
all turn on each other in vicious ways.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:59.920
First, Nancy's ongoing jealousy of Sarah's&nbsp;
natural powers turns into a disaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:04.080
as Sarah tries to guide the group's&nbsp;
growing magic down what she considers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:08.720
healthier paths. As the divide between Nancy&nbsp;
and Sarah grows, Bonnie and Rochelle choose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:08.720 --> 00:13:14.240
the side of power and stick with Nancy, even as&nbsp;
she becomes increasingly erratic and violent.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:18.880
Once Sarah has had enough, the other three&nbsp;
mercilessly bully her just as they've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:23.200
tormented by others, culminating in a&nbsp;
truly grotesque plan to kill Sarah and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:23.200 --> 00:13:27.920
stage it as a suicide. Nancy exploits&nbsp;
vulnerable information about Sarah's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:32.800
suicide attempt — information that was told&nbsp;
to her in confidence — to further torture her.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.800 --> 00:13:37.200
Even after Sarah helps wake Bonnie&nbsp;
and Rochelle up to their bad behavior,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:37.200 --> 00:13:42.640
they still only apologize because they've&nbsp;
lost their powers and want them back.

00:13:42.640 --> 00:13:47.840
"The Craft" ends with Sarah cutting off Rochelle&nbsp;
and Bonnie, while poor Nancy is locked up in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.840 --> 00:13:52.720
a mental institution. If it isn't already&nbsp;
obvious, "The Craft" is more about fraught&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:52.720 --> 00:13:58.400
and toxic relationships between women than&nbsp;
female friends who actually empower each other.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:02.320
If you or anyone you know is&nbsp;
having suicidal thoughts, please&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:11.920
call the National Suicide Prevention&nbsp;
Lifeline at 1-800-273-TALK (8255).

